AWS-018 — Workflow Audit

Document ID: AWS-018
Title: Workflow Audit
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Audit Model (CWAM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Audit Model establishes the principles, structures, evidence requirements, processes, and governance necessary to independently verify Workflow Definitions, Workflow Instances, Workflow Programs, Workflow Orchestration, Monitoring, Optimization, Federation, and related execution activities.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Audit architecture
Audit planning
Audit execution
Evidence collection
Audit findings
Corrective actions
Audit reporting
Continuous assurance

This specification applies to every governed workflow activity within Atlas.

3. Canonical Definition

Workflow Audit is the independent, evidence-based examination of workflow artifacts and execution activities to determine conformity with applicable Atlas specifications, governance requirements, organizational obligations, and engineering standards.

Workflow Audit evaluates execution.

It SHALL NOT modify workflow behavior.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Audit Model SHALL:

Verify workflow integrity.
Verify execution compliance.
Preserve accountability.
Support certification.
Enable continuous assurance.
Preserve immutable evidence.
Support independent review.
Enable reproducibility.
5. Audit Principles

Every workflow audit SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Independence

Audit activities SHALL remain independent of workflow authors, operators, and execution participants.

Evidence-Based

Audit conclusions SHALL rely exclusively upon objective evidence.

Traceability

Every audit finding SHALL reference supporting evidence.

Reproducibility

Equivalent evidence SHALL produce equivalent audit conclusions.

Explainability

Audit findings SHALL include sufficient rationale for independent verification.

Integrity

Audit evidence SHALL remain immutable after collection.

