Audit SHALL remain independent of operational execution.

7. Auditable Activities

Atlas recognizes the following workflow activities as auditable.

Activity	Description
Workflow Authoring	Definition creation and modification
Workflow Approval	Governance approvals
Workflow Distribution	Artifact deployment
Workflow Activation	Instance creation
Workflow Execution	Runtime execution
Workflow Orchestration	Multi-workflow coordination
Workflow Monitoring	Operational observation
Workflow Optimization	Improvement activities
Workflow Federation	Cross-organization execution
Workflow Retirement	End-of-life management

Future specifications MAY introduce additional auditable activities.

8. Audit Planning

Every audit SHALL define:

Property	Description
Audit ID	Unique identifier
Audit Scope	Activities examined
Audit Objectives	Expected outcomes
Audit Criteria	Applicable requirements
Audit Authority	Responsible auditor
Audit Schedule	Planned execution
Audit Method	Manual, automated, or hybrid

Audit plans SHALL be governed Canonical Atlas Objects.

9. Audit Evidence

Every workflow audit SHALL preserve evidence including:

Workflow Definitions
Workflow versions
Workflow execution traces
State transition history
Activity records
Participant assignments
Policy decisions
Monitoring telemetry
Optimization recommendations
Federation agreements
Digital signatures
Canonical Events

Evidence SHALL remain immutable and attributable.

10. Audit Findings

Atlas defines the following canonical finding categories.

Category	Description
Conformant	Requirement satisfied
Observation	Improvement opportunity
Minor Nonconformity	Limited deviation
Major Nonconformity	Significant execution deviation
Critical Nonconformity	Severe execution or governance failure

Findings SHALL reference supporting evidence.

11. Corrective Actions

Every nonconformity SHALL define:

Corrective Action ID
Related finding
Responsible authority
Required remediation
Due date
Verification method
Completion criteria

Corrective actions SHALL remain independently governed.

12. Audit Lifecycle

Every workflow audit SHALL progress through:

Planned
    │
Authorized
    │
Evidence Collected
    │
Evaluated
    │
Findings Issued
    │
Corrective Actions
    │
Verified
    │
Closed
    │
Archived

Lifecycle history SHALL remain immutable.

13. Continuous Assurance

Atlas SHALL support continuous workflow assurance through:

Automated evidence collection
Scheduled reassessments
Workflow change monitoring
Execution drift detection
Risk-triggered audits
Continuous reporting

Continuous assurance SHALL complement—not replace—formal audits.

14. Audit Governance

Every workflow audit SHALL define:

Audit authority
Lead auditor
Independent reviewer
Applicable governance domain
Approval authority
Retention requirements

Audit governance SHALL remain independently auditable.

15. Audit Quality

Every workflow audit SHALL satisfy:

Independence
Completeness
Objectivity
Repeatability
Traceability
Explainability
Timeliness
Auditability

Quality SHALL be continuously measured.

16. Audit Reporting

Every workflow audit report SHALL include:

Audit scope
Assessment criteria
Evidence summary
Findings
Risk assessment
Corrective actions
Overall conclusion
Recommendations

Reports SHALL be reproducible from the recorded evidence.

17. Conformance

A Workflow Audit implementation conforms if it:

Implements canonical audit principles.
Preserves immutable evidence.
Supports independent evaluation.
Produces standardized findings.
Tracks corrective actions.
Maintains audit traceability.
Supports continuous assurance.
18. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-assisted audit planning.
Autonomous evidence verification.
Predictive execution risk analysis.
Cross-federation workflow audits.
Formal audit proofs.
Continuous workflow certification.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical workflow audit semantics.

